<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John III, Burgrave of Nuremberg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1369–<a href="/years/1420">1420</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John III, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgraviate-of-nuremberg">Burgrave of Nuremberg</a>, was a Hohenzollern prince who in the division of 1398 received the Franconian lands 'above the mountains' around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kulmbach">Kulmbach</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/plassenburg">Plassenburg</a>, the later principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayreuth">Bayreuth</a>. He died without sons in 1420, and his lands passed to his brother Frederick, who had already become Elector of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a>.</p></div>
